cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  AxonOS — the open cognitive operating system for
  brain–computer interfaces
message: >-
  If you use AxonOS, its specification, or its verified
  bounds in your work, please cite the project and the
  peer-readable preprint below.
type: software
authors:
  - name: The AxonOS Project
    website: 'https://axonos.org'
  - given-names: Denis
    family-names: Yermakou
repository-code: 'https://github.com/AxonOS-org'
url: 'https://axonos.org'
abstract: >-
  A hard real-time neural operating system for
  brain–computer interfaces: an open-source #![no_std] Rust
  microkernel on ARM Cortex-M with a formally bounded
  worst-case response time, a capability model in which
  raw-cognitive-state permissions do not exist as types,
  and a consent state machine enforced below the
  application layer. Every quantitative claim is graded by
  evidence level (L1 formally proven, L2 measured, L3
  independently validated) and catalogued in CLAIMS.md.
keywords:
  - brain-computer-interface
  - real-time-operating-system
  - formal-verification
  - rust
  - no-std
  - neurotechnology
  - capability-security
  - model-checking
license: Apache-2.0 OR MIT
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  title: >-
    An Analytical Microkernel Design for Safety-Critical
    Brain–Computer Interfaces: Schedulability, Capability
    Isolation, and Falsifiable Predictions
  authors:
    - given-names: Denis
      family-names: Yermakou
  doi: 10.5281/zenodo.20552007
  url: 'https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20552007'
